  "HEY WIND, GET BACK HERE RIGHT NOW! Pip hollered so loud that every cloud and every last wisp of breeze fled over the mountains. The sky went perfectly, uselessly, comically still. Not one kite flew for the rest of the day. Oopsie ending!": '7c9581304bc82b16.mp3',
  "HOOOONK. Every shutter in the city snaps open to complain, spots the one brave lantern on deck, and lights up instead, dock to hilltop, until the clock tower glows last like a period at the end of a very good sentence. Milo toots his tin whistle along with it, because somebody has to conduct. The End!": 'df0d1570890268b7.mp3',
