  "Whisper to the glow": 'b31f3b89533c2a3a.mp3',
  "Who am I?": 'e2addd8b48fc2260.mp3',
  "Whoa \u2014 the lighthouse lamp is SO bright! Luna goes all dizzy and slides right back down to the boat. Home early, blinking little stars. Oopsie ending!": '737ff1fbc112620c.mp3',
  "Whoa! Just testing my battle outfit!": 'cbb879af75f72d2c.mp3',
  "Whooo goes there \u2014 the owl docent swoops overhead with spectacles glinting! Better find cover before those sharp eyes spot Milo.": '6535dc684631aa46.mp3',
  "Whoops, just your reflection stretching its legs!": '3ff3f187146bf95f.mp3',
  "Whoosh down the golden slide": 'bbbdcf216c0bf593.mp3',
  "Whoosh \u2014 the curtain giggles? It's her rain sprite friend, tangled up! 'I came to help \u2014 the curtain won.' Above them, a wobbly little comet laughs so hard it lights up \u2014 and the chandelier catches the giggle-light. Ball time! The End!": 'e952edba6d5d5c57.mp3',
  "Whoosh! The bunny zooms to the moon \u2014 thanks to you!": '42eda16cd989e44b.mp3',
  "Whose shadow is that? Match it!": '6c4d8e325214e9fa.mp3',
  "Wiggle your toes!": 'b739cd9cb03325d2.mp3',
  "Willow grabs the silver bell from the newel post and it FREEZES the room for one second \u2014 useful in a house that will not stop rearranging! One of the paintings is EMPTY with tiny footprints walking away from it, which is NOT how paintings work \u2014 parlor or music room?": 'fd2c79bb5d841587.mp3',
  "Willow sees a BADGER in a top hat peeking at her from behind the curtain, which is never a good sign \u2014 Pumpkin's meow echoes from deeper inside. Library or conservatory?": '923514459c852566.mp3',
  "Willow spots a ball of purple yarn on the floor \u2014 that is Pumpkin's favorite toy, so the cat came THIS way \u2014 and she scoops it up to follow the trail. Spiral staircase or pantry?": '8436a0a92b30d580.mp3',
  "Willow's broomstick just ZOOMED into the bayou like it had somewhere better to be, and her witch exam is at sunrise \u2014 she can see sparks fading in the fog and weird glowing mushroom caps bobbing on the water. Spark trail or mushroom caps?": 'e18cc1c920558a95.mp3',
  "Willow's cat shadow stretched long and SLOW and the broomstick's wild shadow copied it perfectly \u2014 stretch, arch, purr-wiggle. The broomstick drifted down like a leaf and nuzzled her hand because the cat shadow proved she would never yank the handle or take a corner too fast again. The broomstick was never a phantom \u2014 it was a broom that wanted a rider who understood GRACE. Witch exam: passed with flying colors. The End!": '0d665508f24a58ed.mp3',
  "Win them with dancing": '77ee928554d175c5.mp3',
  "Wind gremlins dive-bomb the lantern but Nova snatches a feather cloak off the wall and shields the flame \u2014 the gremlins chitter angrily but the cloak blocks every gust like a tiny windbreaker for fire. Crumbling arch or thunder ridge?": 'edcd5f881a9b6124.mp3',
  "Wind gremlins pour through the gaps and the lantern flame dances wildly \u2014 Nova needs to block one gap FAST with whatever is handy, and this is basically a pillow fort but with rocks and moss. Moss bundle or rock pile?": 'a5ed0d9593b9da78.mp3',
  "Wind the copper key": '3b34767d4f9117c2.mp3',
  "Wind the jade music box": '79e35340d53d6682.mp3',
  "Wind the music box": '9c4eb61b38b53780.mp3',
  "With his lantern covered, Milo was just a warm shadow in the grass. The fireflies swirled overhead, painting slow green spirals, unaware a kitten was hiding right below.": '43ff7be9340b0a55.mp3',
  "With the lantern out, Milo was nothing but moonlight on black fur \u2014 and that turned out to be the most beautiful glow of all. The fireflies stopped fleeing and started wondering.": '3252504f4cfe791f.mp3',
  "Woof woof!": 'ccafeb871b0e052c.mp3',
  "Word spotter! Great listening!": '63d11f364c611d7c.mp3',
  "Wrap up in the scarf": '5db6ef8fa887844d.mp3',
  "Wrapped in the sleeping bag, Milo was basically a purring burrito hurtling through the cosmos. The wandering star kept pace outside, almost like it was waiting for him.": '5cc0f07307987bbc.mp3',
  "Wrapped in the warm cloth, the cog finally stopped shivering and told Milo why it ran \u2014 it loved the clockwork animals too much to lock them still! So Milo wound in a secret hour of freedom at midnight, and the cog purred all the way home. The bells rang at dawn, the mouse danced, and every night the waterfall sings. The End!": '06845cc9556efb9d.mp3',
